{
  "title": "ramekin-core: one shared HTML-fragment-to-text helper; kill \
duplicated and ad-hoc entity decoding",
  "description": "Three related text-cleanup problems in ramekin-core, ordered \
by dependency:\n\
\n\
1. decode_html_entities is duplicated byte-for-byte (same doc comment) in \
src/extract/mod.rs:396 and src/ingredient_parser/item.rs:74. Hoist one copy \
into a shared util module.\n\
\n\
2. src/extract/html_fallback.rs:351-368 and :483-497 hand-roll \
&amp;/&#8217;/&deg;/... replacement chains instead of calling \
decode_html_entities. They miss the vast majority of entities (which leak \
through as raw &...;) and the two chains diverge from each other. Replace both \
with the shared decoder — this is a correctness fix.\n\
\n\
3. There is no shared 'HTML fragment -> clean text' helper: \
HTML_TAG_REGEX.replace_all(x, \"\") followed by varying trim/decode appears \
~15x across blog.rs:52,95,176,341,395,737,866,913,945,952, \
html_fallback.rs:346,481, wprm.rs:98, footnotes.rs:37, each with slightly \
different follow-up. Introduce one fragment_to_text(&str) -> String (strip \
tags + decode + collapse whitespace) and route all call sites through it — \
this is where extractor behavior silently diverges today.\n\
\n\
This changes extraction behavior (fixing entity leakage), so `make pipeline` \
MUST be rerun and the resulting data/ diffs committed — the diffs are the \
point.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
